Origin:
What the Cadence GEM of the
Raspberry Pi 5 (RP1) needs from cemac: MDC divider and RGMII delays set by
the attachment, data bus width from DCFG1, RGMII in USER_IO, zero upper
queue bases on a 64-bit core, a bounded MDIO wait, multicast through the
hash (the perfect filters were written at EMAC offsets), GEM_SA4 at its
real offset, descriptor syncs for a non-coherent bus, a live TX watchdog.

